  "notes": "Bench2Drive 220-route sweep, 6-8 Nov 2026, one RTX PRO 6000 (shared), CARLA 0.9.15, Bench2Drive 7ec25d1 + patches 0001-0002; per_route_timeout_s 5400, no early stop, up to 3 attempts per route (a run that broke in the simulator or the client was set aside and the route driven again). Routes 11715, 11755, 3785, 3800, 23695, 24041, 24071 were driven with patch 0003 as well (the ActorFlow far-car guard), because without it CARLA crashed on them (signal 11, large-map dormancy of a flow car with a collision sensor); the guard acted on 6 (11755, 3785, 3800, 23695, 24041, 24071) of them (`ActorFlow: removed flow car` in evaluator.log) and changes nothing on a route where it does not act. Released NAVSIM-v2 checkpoint (zero-shot on Bench2Drive), momentum-aware selection and the OpenScene crop as model.yaml declares, asked at its own 2 Hz. The sweep loaded the checkpoint from an SSD copy; it is byte-identical to the released checkpoint at the declared {data.navsim.exp} path on the site's hard disk (sha256 740335c800e248598949c2f3c70700da79fe52f5fdc282b887d08fe112d30d05, both checked 8 Nov 2026), so model_env restates the declared value. 22 of 22 source runs kept no run.json, so their routes are attributed to drivejepa on the tree they were found in; config.model_env and the rest of config are what 22/22 source runs recorded. asked for a plan at 2 Hz, the planning_hz the model's model.yaml declared for these runs, the last plan followed in between.",
